WEBVTT

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.030
Huh?

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:19.710
Yotsuya-kun, you haven't turned in your
future plans form yet, have you?

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.650
Oh... y-yeah, uh...

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:25.390
That's right. I heard the
teacher mention that.

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:27.130
So... what are your plans, Shindou-san?

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:29.920
I haven't decided what
job I want or anything,

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:32.720
but I'm going to Morokoshi High
School of Science and Technology.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.550
Same school Kusue's going to.

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:35.890
Oh...

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:38.460
Kusue's thought further
ahead than that, isn't that right?

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:41.740
I want to attend a college with
a pharmaceutical department.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:46.410
I'm hoping... for a career in
pharmaceutical research...

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:48.950
Oh, gosh, why is this so embarrassing?

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:50.860
There's nothing to be embarrassed about!

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:52.620
You can do it for sure, Kusue!

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:53.140
<i>Huh...</i>

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:53.790
You think so?

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:55.040
Yeah! Let's go for it!

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:30.530
Okay, time to find some goblins.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:35.450
Please defeat this troll
and save our village!

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:39.890
At my current rank...

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:41.890
Run! We can't win this one!

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:49.090
At my rank, forget defeating it.

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:52.630
I'd only end up feeding
it, like Shindou-san.

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:57.610
I need to beat some weak monsters
and raise my rank a bit.

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:02.360
A log point?

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:08.280
Hey.

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:09.120
Hakozaki Kusue

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:09.120
Hm?

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:14.210
Shindou Yuu

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:14.210
If we get a guy on our team in the next
round, who do you want it to be?

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:18.130
Hakozaki Kusue

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:18.130
This guy named Yamada-kun.

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:22.050
Shindou Yuu

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:22.050
Oh, the guy who went to the nationals in judo...

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:22.050
Wait, that's not what I mean.

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:24.890
Shindou Yuu

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:24.890
I mean the guy you like.

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:26.510
Hakozaki Kusue

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:26.510
I hate all guys...

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:28.180
What? Why?

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:34.650
Hakozaki Kusue

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:34.650
Well, they're all childish and violent,
and they talk about pervy stuff... I hate it.

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:39.360
Aw, you're such a little kid.
I guess that goes for both of us, though.

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:41.820
Shindou Yuu

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.820
Mine would be...

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:41.820
Yotsuya-kun.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:42.590
Huh?!

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:44.750
No, wait.

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:45.680
That's right!

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:47.910
There are two Yotsuyas in our grade!

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:50.340
Which one?

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:53.500
Shindou Yuu

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:53.500
Well, um...

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:57.500
That one.

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:03.730
Wait! I didn't get to hear it!

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:05.260
Which one did she say?!

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:08.680
<i>But my odds are fifty-fifty.</i>

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:12.350
<i>And I'm basically in a harem scenario
with two girls right now!</i>

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:15.390
<i>Depending on what happens,
one of them might confess to me.</i>

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:17.180
<i>All right!</i>

00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:19.850
Time to get busy!

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:28.000
A forest with a view of the town...

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.740
This takes me back.

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:46.870
Ah, they came to me themselves, huh?

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:54.600
Hideout

00:04:57.150 --> 00:04:59.020
<i>Every time I remember those days...</i>

00:05:01.670 --> 00:05:05.250
<i>everything in my mind goes black with rage.</i>

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:04.610
This is Yotsuya Yuusuke-kun.

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:07.490
I-I just moved here from Kumamoto.

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:11.270
M-My name's Y-Yotsuya Y-Yuusuke.

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:20.730
I missed one! Damn it!

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:26.540
Calm down, man. Don't get so heated.

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:28.840
Rank 9...

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:30.690
And so close to 10.

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:34.510
If I hadn't missed one, I might've made it.

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:38.330
But seriously, isn't there
a way to change jobs?

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:41.620
I'm not stuck in this one forever, am I?

00:05:42.290 --> 00:05:43.190
Nah.

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:46.090
If there are that many
different jobs available,

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:47.900
there must be a way!

00:05:49.670 --> 00:05:52.830
I just wish I had some kind of blade.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:55.670
If Hakozaki-san's the only
one who can use a sword,

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:57.750
<b>Hakozaki Kusue</b>

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:57.750
<b>Warrior (Sword)                   Rank 1</b>

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:57.750
<b></b>Health         > 220%

00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:57.490
there's no point in even having one.

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:00.980
<i>I thought she hated guys...</i>

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:04.910
God, I really wanna be a warri—

00:06:04.910 --> 00:06:05.630
Huh?

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:06.550
<b>Dead</b>

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:06.550
<b>Reviving in</b>

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:08.590
Wait, Hakozaki-san died?!

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:08.590
<b>Dead</b>

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:08.590
<b>Reviving in</b>

00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:12.250
What the hell is she doing?
Isn't she in the village?

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:14.220
Huh?

00:06:17.470 --> 00:06:19.600
Wasn't our quest to...

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:21.860
<b></b>Fulfill the village chief's request

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:24.500
<i>So we... failed the quest?</i>

00:06:27.310 --> 00:06:29.440
<i>And what happens if we fail?</i>

00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:31.090
<i>Do we all die?</i>

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:33.500
<i>Well, regardless!
I have to get to the village!</i>

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:39.710
<b>Dead</b>

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:39.710
<b>Reviving in</b>

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:41.880
<b>Dead</b>

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:41.880
<b>Reviving in</b>

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:41.860
She's staying dead!

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:45.250
Seriously? So Hakozaki-san was eaten, too?!

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:46.290
Which means...

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:49.060
If I die, it'll be for real!

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:54.640
Where are the villagers?

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:57.560
Anyone here?!

00:07:02.140 --> 00:07:03.390
A log point!

00:07:05.310 --> 00:07:07.730
Please, tell me something useful!

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:16.160
Secas

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:16.160
Hey, lady, why do you keep doing practice swings?

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:18.290
Huff... huff...

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:27.920
Hakozaki Kusue

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:24.290
Well, in my own world, I can't do any
strenuous exercise because of my illness...

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:27.920
So this is my first time
swinging something this heavy around...

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:29.510
Secas

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:29.510
Your own world?

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:35.140
I have to take expensive medicine
every month to prevent flare-ups...

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:35.930
Hakozaki Kusue

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:41.860
I know my mom and dad wanted to have
a second child, but with me...

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:45.920
But here, I can move as much as I want
without worrying about my illness,

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:48.850
and I might even be able
to get a little stronger.

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:53.000
But still, all I do is slow
the other two down...

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:54.520
I'm always...

00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:59.400
Ever since I was born, I've been
a burden on so many people.

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:01.640
I have to be, just to stay alive.

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:06.650
So... I want to help everyone
now, while I'm healthy...

00:08:06.650 --> 00:08:07.630
That's why I...

00:08:08.490 --> 00:08:10.660
Wow, sorry. What were you asking about?

00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:12.780
I know none of that made any sense...

00:08:13.770 --> 00:08:15.130
But I'm gonna work hard.

00:08:15.790 --> 00:08:20.030
If anything happens,
I'll keep everyone safe.

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:24.570
<i>I've...</i>

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:30.880
<i>I've been thinking of nothing but
myself since I came here, haven't I?</i>

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:32.230
It's the troll!

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:36.630
Everybody, run! I'll buy you some time!

00:08:36.630 --> 00:08:38.000
<i>No, that's not it.</i>

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:40.950
<i>It's not just since coming here.</i>

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:51.090
<i>I've always been that way.</i>

00:08:51.870 --> 00:08:53.300
Get to safety outside the vil—

00:09:02.190 --> 00:09:03.980
S-Stop!

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:10.490
Shield!

00:09:24.970 --> 00:09:26.620
Help...

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:31.090
Help me,

00:09:31.510 --> 00:09:33.160
Yotsuya-kun...

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:38.450
<i>I...</i>

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:44.830
<i>What do I do? Should I fi—</i>

00:09:44.830 --> 00:09:46.320
<i>No, I have to run!</i>

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:50.730
<i>I can't die now!</i>

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:02.350
<i>I-I'm gonna die! I'm dead!</i>

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:08.000
<b>[Hero Revival Rules]</b>

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:08.000
►When a hero dies, they will revive after
a certain period of time, and the damage
they took will be restored in half that time.
However, if one dies in a situation in which
they would immediately die again upon
revival, such as by drowning in the ocean,
their countdown clock will stop.

00:10:11.190 --> 00:10:14.830
Let's all meet back here after
we graduate from high school

00:10:14.830 --> 00:10:17.250
and dig up this time capsule together!

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:18.020
Okay!

00:10:18.020 --> 00:10:19.980
I promise I'll come back!

00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:22.170
Yeah! We'll be waitin' for ya!

00:10:22.650 --> 00:10:24.670
<i>After graduating from high school...</i>

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:29.820
I'm hoping... for a career in
pharmaceutical research...

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:31.310
<i>Huh...</i>

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:32.980
<i>I never cared.</i>

00:10:34.310 --> 00:10:36.100
<i>It wasn't even on my radar...</i>

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:41.020
Ever since I was born, I've been
a burden on so many people.

00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:43.350
I have to be, just to stay alive.

00:10:43.350 --> 00:10:44.430
So...

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:46.970
<i>Until that moment.</i>

00:10:49.340 --> 00:10:51.460
<i>What the hell?</i>

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:55.510
<i>A kid whose drug costs have been a
burden on her parents wants a job</i>

00:10:55.510 --> 00:10:57.130
<i>in pharmaceutical research?</i>

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:58.920
<i>How obvious can you get?</i>

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:02.180
<i>That's the epitome of a cry
for sympathy, damn it!</i>

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:06.480
<i>And even </i>you<i> are stronger than me?</i>

00:11:06.860 --> 00:11:10.600
<i>Like hell I'm gonna let
someone like that die</i>

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:12.690
<i>at the end of some insane parallel world!</i>

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:16.290
<i>Fine! I'll kick it up one more gear!</i>

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:22.040
<i>There's no way I'm letting someone
who's stronger than me die!</i>

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:25.910
<i>Not then...</i>

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:28.650
<i>and not now!</i>

00:11:37.370 --> 00:11:41.030
<i>His dash only lets him jump like a frog?</i>

00:11:42.830 --> 00:11:43.960
<i>Then...</i>

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:46.640
<i>If I change direction
the moment he jumps...</i>

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:47.810
<i>He can't get me!</i>

00:11:49.150 --> 00:11:51.470
<i>As long as I keep moving, I can shake him!</i>

00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:53.890
<i>I just have to keep moving!</i>

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:03.740
There's no point...

00:12:05.060 --> 00:12:06.690
in just running away!

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:12.450
I need a way to attack him somehow...

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:16.380
<i>Shi—</i>

00:12:22.390 --> 00:12:24.620
Go up!

00:12:33.670 --> 00:12:35.020
<i>He stopped?</i>

00:12:37.490 --> 00:12:39.380
Congratula.

00:12:39.380 --> 00:12:41.200
Your job rank has reached 10.

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:44.710
Yes! I took a gamble and won!

00:12:44.710 --> 00:12:47.860
Wait... Game Master, your voice sounds—

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:51.830
And now it's time to spin the
wheel for the job roul.

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:54.780
Not so fast! I wanted to bask
in my victory for a minute!

00:12:55.160 --> 00:12:56.560
Oh, whatever.

00:12:56.960 --> 00:12:59.160
Something with a blade, please!
A warrior!

00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:01.080
Just let me use a blade!

00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:03.120
Bam!

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:04.720
A chef.

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:10.630
You have gained the following skills
in addition to those you had bef.

00:13:10.630 --> 00:13:11.630
Weak...

00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:13.550
No, wait...

00:13:15.780 --> 00:13:17.720
I got my blade!

00:13:21.990 --> 00:13:22.760
Huh?!

00:13:23.350 --> 00:13:24.870
Is this...

00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:27.450
Can gain knowledge
about edible plants.

00:13:28.020 --> 00:13:30.040
one of my chef skills?

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:33.440
I will now return the flow of time to norm.

00:13:33.440 --> 00:13:34.770
I bid you fare.

00:13:35.450 --> 00:13:36.820
Your stomach...

00:13:37.230 --> 00:13:38.800
is here!

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:42.120
His skin's so tough!

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:45.910
Get through to his stomach!

00:13:50.600 --> 00:13:51.650
How was that?!

00:13:56.560 --> 00:13:58.580
Yes! I can work with this!

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:00.480
<b>Shindou Yuu</b>

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:01.900
<b>Hakozaki Kusue</b>

00:14:07.530 --> 00:14:10.060
It worked... It worked!

00:14:10.060 --> 00:14:11.980
What a relief.

00:14:11.980 --> 00:14:15.210
I wanted to revive, but I'd just
die again inside his stomach,

00:14:15.210 --> 00:14:17.180
so I was totally stuck.

00:14:17.180 --> 00:14:20.200
Yotsuya-kun, you saved us.

00:14:20.680 --> 00:14:22.620
Uh... y-yeah, I guess...

00:14:22.620 --> 00:14:25.500
Wait, are you wearing different clothes?

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:28.360
Oh... My job changed. I'm a chef now.

00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:30.390
What? A chef?

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:34.010
A-Anyway, I figured out this
guy's attack pattern!

00:14:35.570 --> 00:14:37.220
Over here! Hey!

00:14:38.370 --> 00:14:42.990
If you change direction the moment
he jumps, you can dodge him!

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:45.610
That's too much moving around.

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:48.680
With my stats, that would
only work once or twice.

00:14:48.680 --> 00:14:50.620
Not true, actually!

00:14:55.560 --> 00:14:58.130
He's getting tired, too!
From the blood loss?

00:14:58.130 --> 00:15:01.580
A body that size can only
handle so much jumping!

00:15:01.960 --> 00:15:03.290
Let's go, Kusue.

00:15:03.290 --> 00:15:04.510
R-Right!

00:15:06.830 --> 00:15:09.670
Damn, his muscles are so hard!

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:12.780
A lot of good that knowledge does us.

00:15:15.510 --> 00:15:16.890
All right!

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:18.930
<i>What we need is an attack</i>

00:15:19.500 --> 00:15:22.350
<i>strong enough to get through
a troll's defense...</i>

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:24.240
Back again!

00:15:27.600 --> 00:15:29.930
<i>...and none of us has that.</i>

00:15:36.730 --> 00:15:39.750
It seems like we're dying
less often now, at least.

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:43.120
I guess we're getting used
to the way this guy moves.

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:47.800
E-Even if we're dying less, if we can't
beat him, we'll still eventually...

00:15:55.960 --> 00:15:58.610
All wind magic does is move the air.

00:15:58.610 --> 00:16:01.590
And my level's low,
so that's all I can do.

00:16:04.470 --> 00:16:05.510
Shindou-san...

00:16:05.510 --> 00:16:06.150
Huh?

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:10.080
I'll try to land an attack inside
his body through his wound.

00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:11.820
So if you could...

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:15.460
Right, got it.

00:16:18.350 --> 00:16:21.750
<i>His attack range is basically from
his elbow to his fingertips.</i>

00:16:22.110 --> 00:16:23.160
<i>So...</i>

00:16:23.700 --> 00:16:26.910
<i>I'll sacrifice myself to
dive into his belly!</i>

00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:31.400
<i>And now...</i>

00:16:32.180 --> 00:16:34.350
<i>he should stop moving!</i>

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:41.600
<b>Yotsuya Yuusuke</b>

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:41.600
<b>Dead</b>

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:41.600
<b>Reviving in</b>

00:16:44.530 --> 00:16:46.450
So if you could...

00:16:48.820 --> 00:16:50.860
Launch a blast of air...

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:53.540
Wind!

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:54.870
...right into his body!

00:17:06.210 --> 00:17:07.560
We did it!

00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:09.290
That was amazing, Yuu-chan!

00:17:11.930 --> 00:17:12.950
Congrat.

00:17:12.950 --> 00:17:14.060
You scared me!

00:17:14.370 --> 00:17:15.680
You have completed the queue.

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:17.590
O-Oh, right.

00:17:17.590 --> 00:17:20.610
But why do you have to show
up behind me every time?!

00:17:21.890 --> 00:17:22.640
<b>Hakozaki Kusue</b>

00:17:21.900 --> 00:17:23.900
Wow... Our ranks...

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:24.810
<b>Hakozaki Kusue</b>

00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:27.730
<b>Shindou Yuu</b>

00:17:25.170 --> 00:17:28.260
No, my wizard rank hardly went up at all.

00:17:28.260 --> 00:17:30.890
How did the farmer and
chef rank up so much?

00:17:30.890 --> 00:17:31.700
Huh?

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:34.740
<b>Yotsuya Yuusuke</b>

00:17:33.560 --> 00:17:34.730
You're right...

00:17:34.730 --> 00:17:38.270
Now, Chef Yotsuya Yuusuke,

00:17:38.270 --> 00:17:40.060
your reward is the right to ask one ques.

00:17:40.060 --> 00:17:43.160
Again, not so fast!
Give me a minute to bask!

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:47.070
Let's see... What was it...

00:17:47.350 --> 00:17:51.260
When I finished the first one,
I asked him why I was chosen...

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:54.920
<i>Someone we know chose us...</i>

00:17:55.340 --> 00:18:00.420
After the second one, I asked,
"Who are you people?"

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:02.170
<i>He's from the future...</i>

00:18:02.950 --> 00:18:05.610
<i>Does that mean the one
who chose us is, too?</i>

00:18:05.610 --> 00:18:07.100
<i>What are they after, then?</i>

00:18:07.420 --> 00:18:10.950
<i>What is it these people from
the future want us to do?</i>

00:18:12.970 --> 00:18:15.910
The tenth step... After the
tenth step of the quest,

00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:18.900
what will we do?

00:18:18.900 --> 00:18:19.790
Huh?

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:21.020
What?

00:18:21.020 --> 00:18:25.940
Very well. Please watch this version
of what transpired in our wor.

00:18:31.580 --> 00:18:35.010
<i>Is that... our town?</i>

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:42.800
All right! Time for our last summon beast!

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:45.170
Spread out!

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:50.630
Let's go!

00:18:53.780 --> 00:18:55.780
<i>What did I just see?</i>

00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:57.350
What was that?

00:18:58.470 --> 00:19:00.490
W-We're back...

00:19:01.830 --> 00:19:03.750
A-Are we...

00:19:04.460 --> 00:19:06.420
supposed to fight that thing?

00:19:13.450 --> 00:19:15.200
Forget it. I'm going to practice.

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:16.010
Huh?

00:19:16.010 --> 00:19:17.290
Look at the clock.

00:19:18.640 --> 00:19:21.550
The time's the same as it was when we left.

00:19:22.440 --> 00:19:23.940
No, I didn't mean that.

00:19:23.940 --> 00:19:25.220
Is this any time to—

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:29.820
It'll probably be a few weeks
before the next stage begins.

00:19:32.470 --> 00:19:34.850
Now I'll be alive to play
in the tournament.

00:19:34.850 --> 00:19:38.280
I'm just glad my two years of
hard work won't go to waste!

00:19:38.670 --> 00:19:40.530
Thank you so much!

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:41.960
S-Sure...

00:19:41.960 --> 00:19:45.560
<i>That's right... We're third-years,
so her next match is her last.</i>

00:19:45.560 --> 00:19:47.210
Okay, I'm off.

00:19:47.210 --> 00:19:50.370
Yotsuya-kun, make sure you
get Kusue home safe.

00:19:51.420 --> 00:19:52.210
Huh?

00:19:59.350 --> 00:20:02.070
<i>My heart is still pounding.</i>

00:20:03.390 --> 00:20:05.960
<i>We were in that world for more than a day,</i>

00:20:05.960 --> 00:20:08.730
<i>but no time passed in this world at all.</i>

00:20:09.220 --> 00:20:12.870
<i>And if we don't make it through
that seven more times...</i>

00:20:14.360 --> 00:20:16.690
<i>We'll all die.</i>

00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:18.290
Um...

00:20:18.620 --> 00:20:20.700
I want to thank you.

00:20:20.700 --> 00:20:24.530
If you hadn't shown up, we would've died.

00:20:24.530 --> 00:20:25.740
<i>Wait...</i>

00:20:25.740 --> 00:20:29.920
<i>Have I ever walked alone
with a girl before?</i>

00:20:29.920 --> 00:20:31.490
<i>In my entire life?</i>

00:20:32.180 --> 00:20:35.860
W-Well, you know... we were
all in the same boat.

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:41.950
I mean, people say, "I'll protect you,"
all the time these days, right?

00:20:41.950 --> 00:20:44.370
Uh... I wouldn't know.

00:20:44.370 --> 00:20:46.940
I never liked that kind of thing.

00:20:46.940 --> 00:20:51.030
I'm kind of a contrarian... like, I
hate the stuff that most people love.

00:20:51.800 --> 00:20:55.180
<i>Wait... I'm saying stuff I
really don't need to say.</i>

00:20:56.150 --> 00:20:58.270
But in that world,

00:20:58.270 --> 00:21:02.640
keeping at least one person alive
benefits all of us, so...

00:21:02.640 --> 00:21:06.060
I feel like that kinda fits me, y'know?

00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:08.130
Really?

00:21:08.480 --> 00:21:11.810
<i>I really don't need to be
telling her any of this!</i>

00:21:20.480 --> 00:21:22.170
<i>That was when I realized...</i>

00:21:25.650 --> 00:21:28.380
<i>If I abandon the quest,</i>

00:21:28.920 --> 00:21:33.670
<i>there's a chance that this city I
hate so much could be destroyed.</i>

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:40.020
<b>This City I Hate So Much</b>

00:23:09.990 --> 00:23:12.660
Subquest 2

00:23:09.990 --> 00:23:12.660
<b>Close in on Yotsuya's reality.</b>

00:23:13.740 --> 00:23:15.830
What are your thoughts on Yotsuya-kun?

00:23:15.830 --> 00:23:17.790
Huh? My thoughts on Yotsuya-kun?

00:23:17.790 --> 00:23:19.490
He's pretty hot, right?

00:23:19.490 --> 00:23:22.410
I think he's someone who can be trusted.

00:23:22.410 --> 00:23:24.140
He's a good guy.

00:23:24.140 --> 00:23:27.790
Like, I guess he's the kind of
guy you'd call a protagonist.

00:23:24.590 --> 00:23:28.130
I guess he's
the kind of guy you'd call a protagonist

00:23:28.120 --> 00:23:30.550
My thoughts on Yotsuya-kun? As in...

00:23:30.550 --> 00:23:33.850
The Yotsuya-kun who's hot,
a good guy, and worthy of trust.

00:23:33.840 --> 00:23:35.360
Oh, that one?

00:23:33.850 --> 00:23:38.270
<b>The 13 Methods You Need
to Become the Strongest Warrior</b>

00:23:35.360 --> 00:23:38.270
I haven't really talked to
him much, so I'm not sure.

00:23:38.270 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>End
</b>Production:<b></b>
